# Only backend/ai/mcp/Dockerfile and cron/Dockerfile build from the repo root,
# and they need just backend/ and cron/.  Everything else stays out of the build
# context - in production the repo root also holds pgdata/ (the live Postgres
# data directory), backups/, redis_data/ and node_modules, which made the
# context gigabytes and the mcp build take hours.
*
!backend
!cron

# Never bake secrets into an image layer.  backend/ai/mcp/Dockerfile COPYs
# backend/ wholesale, so without this backend/.env - holding MCP_KEY as well as
# TELEGRAF_KEY - ends up baked into the mcp image.  The mcp service bind-mounts
# ./backend over /app/backend at runtime, so the real .env is still there.
**/.env

# Runtime data and build/test output - bind-mounted or regenerated, never needed
# in an image
backend/uploads
backend/output-labyrinth
backend/htmlcov
**/__pycache__
**/.coverage*
**/.pytest_cache
